# Data Layer Rules (BookShelf)

- Keep all JSON file I/O in this layer only; routes and services must never call `fs` directly.
- `jsonStore.ts` is the only place that should use `fs.readFile` and `fs.writeFile`.
- Repository modules should expose CRUD-style operations for callers, not raw file utilities.
- Follow full-document write behavior: read array, mutate in memory, write the full array back.
- Do not introduce partial writes, file streaming, locks, or concurrency control.
- Keep id conventions consistent when creating entities:
  - `book_` + 8 hex chars
  - `shelf_` + 8 hex chars
  - `review_` + 8 hex chars
- Treat `data/books.json` seed records as persistent baseline data; do not delete seeded books.
